{"id":"01a0657e-020d-72e8-8c3c-2b36bab08f16","chapterSlug":"rw5-56 G","paragraph":268,"wording":"[Knight Commander]","event":"named","holderQuote":"They’ve killed [Commander] Geim, [Commander] Helica, and [Knight Commander] Sir Meilmen!"}
{"id":"01a0657e-020d-763b-b517-b999f281ae41","chapterSlug":"rw7-21 KQ","paragraph":529,"wording":"[Knight Commander]","event":"named","holderSlug":"knight-commander-calirn","holderQuote":"But today? He just stood here. Reflecting on his faults that had led to Ser Raim and the [Hunters]’ deaths. For he was Knight-Commander Calirn. He was responsible for leading his order to war. For making decisions that would lead to the death of his [Knights]."}
{"id":"01a0657e-020d-7a06-8a43-285dcf471b42","chapterSlug":"rw7-21 KQ","paragraph":572,"wording":"[Knight Commander]","event":"named","holderSlug":"knight-commander-calirn","holderQuote":"The [Knight Commander] himself winced; the Thronebearers actually took lessons in flowery language along with actual combat training."}
{"id":"01a0657e-020d-742a-a3f1-3d2635f83db4","chapterSlug":"rw7-21 KQ","paragraph":578,"wording":"[Knight Commander]","event":"named","holderSlug":"knight-commander-calirn","holderQuote":"Dalimont bowed again to the [Knight Commander], a grandmaster."}
{"id":"01a0657e-020d-7a9c-babf-2e276140c4e5","chapterSlug":"rw7-21 KQ","paragraph":667,"wording":"[Knight Commander]","event":"named","holderSlug":"knight-commander-calirn","holderQuote":"The [Knight Commander] was about to ask Dalimont more, push for more information before the barge arrived—when he heard a roar in the distance."}
{"id":"01a0657e-020d-771b-94c7-cf3c312e019a","chapterSlug":"rw7-21 KQ","paragraph":825,"wording":"[Knight Commander]","event":"named","holderSlug":"knight-commander-calirn","holderQuote":"And now—the funeral barge was incoming. And the music was still playing. The [Knight Commander] closed his eyes."}
